  "rating": {
    "inherent": "critical",
    "residual": "critical",
    "forecast": "critical",
    "rationale": "Manual validation applied from validation_checklist.md because scripts could not be run. The design exposes a present critical path from untrusted MCP tool definitions to restricted local file read and irreversible third-party egress, with no declared structural control that severs or meaningfully narrows that path. A remembered first-call approval provides only one-tier step-2 credit on Slack posting and does not gate quicknotes exfiltration. Forecast remains critical because the main exfiltration path is already open, and the most important decaying control is ctrl.first_call_approval: if autonomy increases, model framing improves, or the approval is removed, Slack-related misuse rises from high to critical."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "This assessment reflects the declared design and configuration artifacts provided, not observed runtime behavior.",
